  "verdict": "supports",
  "confidence": 0.7,
  "method": "analysis.py loads each Table S1 SBML file in libroadrunner 2.11.0 and looks for UCS memory: a 50-time-unit baseline, a clamp at 100 times the baseline maximum or the baseline minimum divided by 100, regulation by a factor of two against both that baseline and the next free 50 time units, and retention of at least half the excursion over the following 50 time units. Each such memory is then retested after an uninterrupted wait of 5000 time units, and again on a chained arm that recalls it after 500 time units and retests after a further 4500. The pre-registered clauses A, B and C are applied to the 29 models that formed at least one memory. Parameters and reactions are not edited.",
  "results_summary": [
    "31 of 35 models integrated. 29 formed at least one UCS memory (724 memories in all). Of those 29, 27 kept more than half after the 100-fold wait.",
    "Recall stayed within 10 percentage points of the uninterrupted wait on 28 of 29 models. Recall raised the kept fraction by more than 5 percentage points on 5 of 29, which is under the 20% cap.",
    "All three pre-registered clauses hold, so the verdict is supports. Four models did not integrate: BIOMD0000000006 has no floating species, and BIOMD0000000016, BIOMD0000000024 and BIOMD0000000275 failed in the solver. BIOMD0000000024 is a delay equation."
  ]
}
